        "$value": "color-mix(in oklab, {color.qeet.500} 13%, transparent)",
        "$type": "color",
        "$description": "Translucent in dark, unlike light: a selected row has to read as a Qeet tint on whatever it sits on — card, popover, sidebar — and dark surfaces step in lightness, so a tint mixed into one of them reads recessed on a lighter one. Over surface.default it is exactly the old opaque mix. The feedback *-subtle tints work the same way."
